# Cloudflare Pages security headers (Doctrine §16.6).
#
# THERE IS A CONTENT-SECURITY-POLICY NOW, and it cost a header rather than a
# refactor because this app has never carried a single inline script or inline
# style. That was preserved on purpose — it is why `theme.js` is an external
# blocking file rather than the inline one-liner PALETTES.md suggests — and this
# is what that decision was being kept for.
#
# The policy is DENY-BY-DEFAULT and every allowance below is something the app
# genuinely does:
#
#   script-src    theme.js and the ES module. No inline, no eval, no wasm.
#   style-src     styles.css. Custom properties set through the CSSOM are not
#                 covered by style-src, so the histogram's --fill and theme.js's
#                 colorScheme need nothing here.
#   img-src       the SVG icons. No data: URIs anywhere in this app.
#   connect-src   the service worker fetching what it precaches. Same origin
#                 only, which is also the runtime no-network claim written as a
#                 rule the browser enforces rather than a promise.
#   worker-src    sw.js.
#   manifest-src  the webmanifest.
#   form-action   'none'. Every form here is submitted through JavaScript and
#                 the default prevented; if that ever fails, this stops the
#                 navigation rather than letting the page post somewhere.
#   font-src      'none'. System fonts only.
#
# AND THE PERMISSIONS-POLICY DENIES EVERYTHING THE BROWSER OFFERS, one feature
# at a time, rather than listing the frightening ones. Camera and microphone are
# what a person asks about; the list below also refuses the ones nobody thinks
# to ask about — idle detection, window management, local font enumeration,
# topics — because those are the ones that would arrive quietly.
#
# `clipboard-write=(self)` is the ONE allowance, and it is what the copy buttons
# need. Writing to the clipboard on a click needs no prompt; reading it is
# denied outright, which is the half that could see something a student did not
# mean to give.
#
# `tools/permissions-check.mjs` holds this list against the bundle: it fails if
# any code that could prompt for a permission appears, and it fails if a feature
# on its list stops being denied here.
#
# `tools/serve.mjs` parses this file and serves what it declares, so the journey
# walk and the accessibility gate both run UNDER this policy on every run. A
# policy nothing exercises is a policy discovered by a class.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; worker-src 'self'; manifest-src 'self'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'; font-src 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), ambient-light-sensor=(), autoplay=(), bluetooth=(), browsing-topics=(), camera=(), display-capture=(), encrypted-media=(), gamepad=(), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), hid=(), idle-detection=(), interest-cohort=(), local-fonts=(), magnetometer=(), microphone=(), midi=(), payment=(), picture-in-picture=(), publickey-credentials-get=(), screen-wake-lock=(), serial=(), storage-access=(), usb=(), window-management=(), xr-spatial-tracking=(), clipboard-read=(), clipboard-write=(self)

# The worker must never be served from a cache older than itself, or a new
# release cannot arrive at all.
/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/precache.json
  Cache-Control: no-cache
